<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n114277" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χοῖνιξ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῐκος</span>, ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>choenix,</i> a dry measure, esp. for corn, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.192
			</span></i>, etc.; the <i>choenix</i> of corn was one man's daily
			allowance, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				7.187
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ γὰρ χ. ἡμερησία τροφή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.L.
					8.18
				</span></i>
			; given to slaves, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.16
			</span></i>; hence, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅς κεν ἐμῆς γε χοίνικος
				ἅπτηται,</span> i. e. whoever eats of my <i>bread,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				19.28
			</span></i>: prov., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ χοίνικος
			καθέζεσθαι,</span> i. e. sit idle, live in idleness, <i><span class="en">
				Pythag.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				197
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.703f
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				10.452e
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>VH</u>
				1.26
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδὲ τὴν χ. ἔτι λήψει</span>
			(of gold) <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Nav.</u>
				27
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χ. Ἀττική</span> (<i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>/<i><span class="en">
				48
			</span></i> of the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέδιμνος</span>
			=
			<i><span class="en">
				4
			</span></i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοτύλαι</span>) <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				1.5.6
			</span></i>; in Pap. usu. abbreviated <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χ</span>, as
			in <i><span class="en">
				<u>PCair.Zen.</u>
				645.11
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B. C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				1044.3
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A. D.)</span>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> from the like ness of shape, a kind of
				<i>stocks</i> for fastening the legs, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pl.</u>
				276
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				18.129
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χοινικίς</span>
			 VI, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PCair.Zen.</u>
				782
			</span></i><i>a.</i><i><span class="en">
				7
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B. C.)</span>, prob. in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Supp.Epigr.</u>
				4.447.48
			</span></i> (Didyma, <span class="entity">ii B. C.</span>).</div>
